<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Nu'man III ibn al-Mundhir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 602</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Nu'man III ibn al-Mundhir was the last Lakhmid king of al-Hira, reigning from about 582 until 602 as a client of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>. A Christian of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-east">Church of the East</a> and a patron of poets such as al-Nabigha, he fell out with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-ii">Khosrow II</a>, who had him imprisoned and put to death. The end of the Lakhmid buffer state weakened Persian control of the desert frontier and was followed by the Arab victory at Dhi Qar.</p></div>
